(4836321, 701312, 90372, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful idea but the depth of field is a little shallow. You can avoid shallow depth of field in the future by shooting at 50-55mm, that''s where you can obtain maximum DOF. You can always crop it to your subject in post processing. However, If your depth of field choice was deliberate it''s a good execution of artistic license. 6</td>', 'This is a wonderful idea but the depth of field is a little shallow. You can avoid shallow depth of field in the future by shooting at 50-55mm, that''s where you can obtain maximum DOF. You can always crop it to your subject in post processing. However, If your depth of field choice was deliberate it''s a good execution of artistic license. 6', '2008-07-21 03:43:11.000000', NULL, 1),
