(4852537, 700757, 71105, '<td valign="top">Looks familiar...<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=584479" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/739/120/584479.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/739/120/584479.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/739/120/584479.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Granted, your new one is much better than my old one, but I am still learning.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-30 23:21:40.</i></td>', 'Looks familiar...   Granted, your new one is much better than my old one, but I am still learning.', '2008-07-31 00:20:11.000000', '2008-07-31 00:21:40.000000', 0),
(4852691, 701110, 11716, '<td valign="top">Fantastic image and worthy of the ribbon it(you) earned.  I have a different take on your OOF concerns. Like all good macro photography, what you intended to have in crisp focus was in crisp focus, that being the drop of the bottom of the spoon and its amazing reflection in on the surface of the coffee.  The texture of the sugar toward the rear of the cube really completes the the image.  So, while you see this as an f16 photo with a slight focus problem, I see it as a perfectly composed f2 macro shot.  My favorite in the challenge for sure...</td>', 'Fantastic image and worthy of the ribbon it(you) earned.  I have a different take on your OOF concerns. Like all good macro photography, what you intended to have in crisp focus was in crisp focus, that being the drop of the bottom of the spoon and its amazing reflection in on the surface of the coffee.  The texture of the sugar toward the rear of the cube really completes the the image.  So, while you see this as an f16 photo with a slight focus problem, I see it as a perfectly composed f2 macro shot.  My favorite in the challenge for sure...', '2008-07-31 01:24:08.000000', NULL, 0),
