(4854890, 701242, 83080, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot and congratualtions on your patience as well.  The 50mm/1.8 works well and if you get into this IreneM style you might consider investing in a <a href="//dpchallenge.com/lens.php?LENS_ID=1088" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Tamron SP AF 90mm f/2.8 Di</a> which she has used for many of her great drop shots.  I purchased one a while ago and fell in love with it the first time I used it.</td>', 'Excellent shot and congratualtions on your patience as well.  The 50mm/1.8 works well and if you get into this IreneM style you might consider investing in a Tamron SP AF 90mm f/2.8 Di which she has used for many of her great drop shots.  I purchased one a while ago and fell in love with it the first time I used it.', '2008-08-01 04:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4855676, 700757, 78516, '<td valign="top">I''m typing this from a public hotel computer because we''re on vacation, but I just wanted to respond to this. <br/> <br/>It''s totally FREAKY how much these two photos look alike, but I can honestly say that I don''t recall ever seeing the other photo until yesterday. My shot was not copied from anyone. I know that sounds hard to believe because they look SO much alike, but it''s nothing more than a weird coincidence. Those sucker shots aren''t uncommon, in fact there was another one in this challenge. <br/> <br/>I know it doesn''t really matter in the long run, I just don''t want to be accused of copying someone elses work when I know that I didn''t. I''m going to go back to my vacation now, so if you want to discuss it further you''re going to have to wait until Sunday when I get home.</td>', 'I''m typing this from a public hotel computer because we''re on vacation, but I just wanted to respond to this.  It''s totally FREAKY how much these two photos look alike, but I can honestly say that I don''t recall ever seeing the other photo until yesterday. My shot was not copied from anyone. I know that sounds hard to believe because they look SO much alike, but it''s nothing more than a weird coincidence. Those sucker shots aren''t uncommon, in fact there was another one in this challenge.  I know it doesn''t really matter in the long run, I just don''t want to be accused of copying someone elses work when I know that I didn''t. I''m going to go back to my vacation now, so if you want to discuss it further you''re going to have to wait until Sunday when I get home.', '2008-08-01 11:20:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4856324, 700757, 71105, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Wenders11:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m typing this from a public hotel computer because we''re on vacation, but I just wanted to respond to this. <br/> <br/>It''s totally FREAKY how much these two photos look alike, but I can honestly say that I don''t recall ever seeing the other photo until yesterday. My shot was not copied from anyone. I know that sounds hard to believe because they look SO much alike, but it''s nothing more than a weird coincidence. Those sucker shots aren''t uncommon, in fact there was another one in this challenge. <br/> <br/>I know it doesn''t really matter in the long run, I just don''t want to be accused of copying someone elses work when I know that I didn''t. I''m going to go back to my vacation now, so if you want to discuss it further you''re going to have to wait until Sunday when I get home. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wendy, I''m not accusing you of anything.  I was actually complimenting you on pulling off a better shot of the one I tried to do.  I''m not surprised that someone else had the same idea for a similar shot.  To think that I would be the only one to think of this concept would be quite egotistical.  I was merely pointing out the strange coincidence that our minds had come up with on different occasions.  Plus, if you were to copy a photographer, I would suggest someone else, like Librodo, anyway.  :)</td>', 'Originally posted by Wenders11: I''m typing this from a public hotel computer because we''re on vacation, but I just wanted to respond to this.  It''s totally FREAKY how much these two photos look alike, but I can honestly say that I don''t recall ever seeing the other photo until yesterday. My shot was not copied from anyone. I know that sounds hard to believe because they look SO much alike, but it''s nothing more than a weird coincidence. Those sucker shots aren''t uncommon, in fact there was another one in this challenge.  I know it doesn''t really matter in the long run, I just don''t want to be accused of copying someone elses work when I know that I didn''t. I''m going to go back to my vacation now, so if you want to discuss it further you''re going to have to wait until Sunday when I get home.   Wendy, I''m not accusing you of anything.  I was actually complimenting you on pulling off a better shot of the one I tried to do.  I''m not surprised that someone else had the same idea for a similar shot.  To think that I would be the only one to think of this concept would be quite egotistical.  I was merely pointing out the strange coincidence that our minds had come up with on different occasions.  Plus, if you were to copy a photographer, I would suggest someone else, like Librodo, anyway.  :)', '2008-08-01 13:15:29.000000', NULL, 0),
